<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    
    <h2>What Is the Snickers® Blizzard® Treat?</h2>
    <p>The Snickers® Blizzard is the most texturally complex of the candy-bar Blizzards. A Snickers bar contains four distinct elements — chocolate coating, caramel, nougat, and peanuts — and all four make their presence known when blended into soft serve. You get crunch from peanuts, chew from nougat and caramel, and chocolate throughout. It is more satisfying per spoonful than the simpler <a href="/items/mm-blizzard">M&amp;M's</a> or <a href="/items/butterfinger-blizzard">Butterfinger</a> Blizzards.</p>
  <p>See the full DQ menu at <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a> or browse all flavors on the <a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">Blizzard Treats page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Why Snickers Works Well in a Blizzard</h2>
  <p>Snickers is one of the better candy bars to blend into soft serve because its layered structure means different elements break apart and distribute differently during blending. Peanuts hold their shape for crunch. Nougat dissolves partially and adds chew. Caramel creates pockets of sweetness throughout. Chocolate coating disperses into the soft serve for depth. No single candy-bar Blizzard gives you more variety in each spoonful.</p>
  <h2>Allergen Note</h2>
  <p>The Snickers® Blizzard contains peanuts and tree nuts. Not suitable for guests with peanut or nut allergies. Consider the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> or <a href="/items/mm-blizzard">M&amp;M's Blizzard</a> as nut-free alternatives.</p>

    <h2>How It Compares to Other Blizzards</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Flavor Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Snickers® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>500</td><td>Peanuts + caramel + nougat + chocolate</td></tr><tr><td>Turtle Pecan Cluster</td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>570</td><td>Pecans + caramel + fudge</td></tr><tr><td>M&amp;M's® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>490</td><td>Simpler candy crunch</td></tr><tr><td>Butterfinger® Blizzard</td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>470</td><td>Crispy PB wafer, no nougat</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>First timer?</strong> Order a Mini (3.49) — it's 4–5 spoonfuls, perfect for a taste test before committing to a full cup.</li>
      <li><strong>Best size for one person:</strong> Small (4.49) at 500 calories hits the sweet spot of satisfaction without going overboard.</li>
      <li><strong>Upgrade option:</strong> Ask to blend in a hot fudge swirl for richer chocolate depth, or add extra mix-ins (~$0.50).</li>
      <li><strong>Check the flip:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down — if your crew doesn't flip it, it's free.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Related Blizzard Treats &amp; Menu Items</h2><ul><li><a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard</a></li><li><a href="/items/reeses-blizzard">Reese's® Blizzard</a></li><li><a href="/items/mm-blizzard">M&amp;M's® Blizzard</a></li><li><a href="/categories/blizzard-treats">All Blizzard Treats</a></li></ul>
    
